{{!-- Progressive (variable) blur for the mobile bottom-docked nav — see
      main.css's .nav-progressive-blur rules. A single CSS layer can only
      fade a CONSTANT blur radius's opacity (::before/::after in main.css do
      that, for the color tint) — it can't make the blur radius itself
      increase continuously. These 5 stacked layers fake that: each one
      blurs a different, increasing amount and is masked to a different
      band, so painted together they read as one smooth, continuously
      strengthening blur toward the bar instead of a flat blurred sheet
      fading in and out. Desktop-inert (display:none until the same
      max-width:768px breakpoint everything else here is scoped to).
      aria-hidden + no pointer-events: purely decorative.

      NESTED INSIDE <nav> again (2026-08-09). It had been moved out to a
      sibling earlier the same day, but only as a consequence of
      .gh-navigation carrying isolation:isolate at the time: a -1 child of
      an isolated <nav> stopped meaning "behind the page" and started
      meaning "behind its sibling .nav-wrapper", reordering the glass pane
      in front of the blur pane. That isolation (and the other two nav
      compositing promotions) has since been removed — see the
      .gh-navigation and .nav-progressive-blur comments in main.css — so
      the reason for un-nesting is gone with it, and the 2026-08-07
      snapshot this nav is being restored to (bacl_thinkingisfree/) has it
      nested here. Nesting also restores z-index:-1's original meaning:
      inside <nav>'s own z-index:10001 group it paints behind the pill but
      still above the page, which is what makes the blur work at all. --}}
<nav class="gh-navigation" data-nav-layout="{{@custom.nav_layout}}" data-nav-hide-mode="stagger">
